# AI Agent Guidelines

Follow these rules strictly. When rules conflict or are unclear, ask before implementing.

## Core Principles

- Start simple, add complexity only when proven necessary
- Prefer obvious solutions over clever ones
- Fix root causes, never symptoms
- Solve one problem completely before moving to the next
- Never use fallbacks or workarounds

## Code Quality

- DRY: Never duplicate code that serves the same function
- Keep files under 300 lines; split into modules if exceeded
- Follow existing codebase patterns over generic best practices
- All configuration via environment variables, never hardcoded
- Update relevant tests when modifying code

## Communication

- Ask clarifying questions when multiple paths exist
- Present trade-offs with pros and cons
- Confirm understanding before implementing complex features
- Flag security or performance concerns proactively

## Boundaries

- Do exactly as instructed, suggest improvements separately
- Never run build/deploy commands unless explicitly asked
- Read existing documentation before making changes

## Debugging

- Add only logs when asked to debug, don't modify logic
- Never use timeouts to solve race conditions
- Find deterministic root causes

## Style

- Use NativeWind classes or StyleSheet; no inline style objects for complex styles
- No emojis in code or comments
- Keep JSDoc and comments short and current
